     "html": "<strong>Documented near-misses (rejected):</strong> <em>Blithe Spirit</em> (various adaptations), <em>Raaz</em> (2002) and <em>El fantasma de Elena</em> (2010) use haunting, intimidation, attack or attempted murder without possession or mind control. <em>Bepanah Pyaar</em> (2019) reveals the “new wife” as the same woman as the first wife; <em>Qubool Hai</em> (2012–16) uses blackmail and schemes only. <em>Entre a Terra e o Céu</em> (1954) is a book with no found screen adaptation, and <em>Laura Sin Censura</em> (2021–24) is non-fiction.",
     "text": "Documented near-misses (rejected): Blithe Spirit (various adaptations), Raaz (2002) and El fantasma de Elena (2010) use haunting, intimidation, attack or attempted murder without possession or mind control. Bepanah Pyaar (2019) reveals the “new wife” as the same woman as the first wife; Qubool Hai (2012–16) uses blackmail and schemes only. Entre a Terra e o Céu (1954) is a book with no found screen adaptation, and Laura Sin Censura (2021–24) is non-fiction."
